{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112102,"nonce":"WVf0vBGeN+l6S1Ev0zS0Dd1ufiw=","title":"4.1 Playbook: lessons, morning checklist, post-mortems","message":"Wave 4 — play. Depends: 1.2 (journal is the post-mortem input). Shapes 4.2/4.3.\n\n## Goal\nThe learning system: versioned playbook (lessons), the morning checklist, and\nthe post-mortem procedure that turns journal history into all of the above.\nThis is agent behavior design, not C#.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Learning §Observation (upkeep layer)\n- The auto-memory system's shape (one fact per file + index) — proven pattern\n- 1.2 journal schema; 1.4 transcript dirs\n\n## Scope\n- `playbook/`: one lesson per file — frontmatter (name, trigger-context,\n  confidence, source-run) + body (what, why, how-to-apply). INDEX.md.\n- `checklists/morning.md` v1 authored now from DESIGN's upkeep layer (food-\n  days, apparel HP% vs stockpile vs season, mood trends, meds, power margin,\n  fire coverage, defense readiness) — each item: what to query (rwa command)\n  + what threshold warrants action.\n- `templates/`: parametric layout starters (bedroom, freezer+kitchen, power\n  room — power room includes the firefoam popper, the canonical pre-learned\n  lesson) as IR generators or annotated IR.\n- `postmortem.md`: the procedure — inputs (journal, transcripts, save), steps\n  (timeline of harm → root cause → prevention), outputs (lesson file, and/or\n  checklist item, and/or template patch), escalation ladder (prose → checklist\n  → template) with criteria for promotion.\n- Session-start contract: what 4.2's loop loads and in what order.\n\n## Invariants\nLessons cite their source run; checklist items name their query; templates\ncarry their lessons as comments (why the popper is there).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nFrontmatter schema; promotion criteria; how conflicting lessons resolve\n(newer wins? confidence field?); template parameter format.\n\n## Acceptance\nDry-run: given a scripted journal from a lost colony (fire spread from\nunpoppered generator — construct via dev verbs or synthetically), following\npostmortem.md yields a correct lesson file AND a checklist item AND a template\npatch; a fresh session's documented load order would surface all three.","files":null}]}